September 12th, 1774

Rode out to the ridge this morning to clear my head. The sky was low, cloudy — smelled like rain but never came.
Sometimes I wonder if Rock Ridge can really last, or if we’re just putting off the inevitable.

Bart’s got a lead on something... some paper Taggart dropped while bumbling around the freight yard. Says there’s
coordinates on it. I haven’t seen it myself, but I trust the man. If he says there’s more to it, there is.

We spent the afternoon in the jailhouse going over some old maps. Real dusty stuff. But something caught my eye:
a series of numbers scribbled faintly on the back of one. Weren’t no marking I recognized — looked more like code.

No doubt in my mind now: Lamarr’s not acting alone. Somebody, somewhere, is pulling strings.

- Jim “The Waco Kid”
